{
  "notesForUsage": [
    "Every LLM this stack knows how to talk to, by name, and which one it is using.",
    "",
    "This is the committed sample. `just setup` copies it to `llm.json`, which is gitignored and",
    "is what actually runs — so your choice of model is yours and never shows up as a change to",
    "the repository. Edit `llm.json`, not this file, unless you are changing what a fresh clone",
    "should start with.",
    "",
    "Change `active` and restart the Runtime (`just restart runtime`) — that is the whole switch.",
    "No secret belongs in either file: each profile's key is read from `.env` under a variable",
    "named after the profile, so `azure_gpt` takes AZURE_GPT_KEY. Adding a profile means adding an",
    "entry here and one line to `.env`; nothing else in the stack has to know its name.",
    "",
    "Fields: provider (openai | anthropic | scripted), baseUrl, model, temperature (optional),",
    "requiresKey (optional; set false for a server that wants no key at all — an mlx/omlx server",
    "does want one, so `local_qwen` reads LOCAL_QWEN_KEY like any other profile), scriptFile",
    "(scripted only). `Assistant.LlmModel` overrides `model` for that one Assistant.",
    "",
    "There is a second, optional switch: `vision`, a sibling of `active`, naming the profile that",
    "`document.readScan` sends a scanned PDF to. Leave it out — as this file does — and there is no",
    "vision model: reading a scan is unavailable and an Assistant that meets a PDF with no text",
    "layer asks the User to type what it says instead. Set it, and that profile needs its own key",
    "in `.env` exactly like any other, so `vision_claude` reads VISION_CLAUDE_KEY. Only `anthropic`",
    "profiles can read a scan today. To turn it on, add a profile under `profiles`:",
    "",
    "    \"vision_claude\": {",
    "      \"provider\": \"anthropic\",",
    "      \"baseUrl\": \"https://api.anthropic.com\",",
    "      \"model\": \"claude-opus-5\"",
    "    }",
    "",
    "and then the line `\"vision\": \"vision_claude\",` next to `\"active\"` below.",
    "",
    "See README.md, 'The language model'."
  ],

  "active": "scripted",

  "profiles": {
    "scripted": {
      "provider": "scripted",
      "model": "scripted",
      "scriptFile": "/run/fixtures/llm-script.json"
    },

    "openai": {
      "provider": "openai",
      "baseUrl": "https://api.openai.com/v1",
      "model": "gpt-4o-mini"
    },

    "anthropic": {
      "provider": "anthropic",
      "baseUrl": "https://api.anthropic.com",
      "model": "claude-sonnet-4-5"
    },

    "azure_gpt": {
      "provider": "openai",
      "baseUrl": "https://YOUR-RESOURCE.openai.azure.com/openai/v1",
      "model": "gpt-4o"
    },

    "local_qwen": {
      "provider": "openai",
      "baseUrl": "http://host.docker.internal:8000/v1",
      "model": "Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct-4bit",
      "temperature": 0
    }
  }
}
